     "text": "CLINICAL SUMMARY - Taylor-Chandler Medical Group\nPatient: Brandon Price DOB: 02/12/1969 Sex: M MRN: 673923\n\nEncounters:\n 2025-01-13 HIV BP 120/81 Wt 232\n 2024-10-15 HIV BP 132/81 Wt 240\n 2024-07-17 URI BP 124/89 Wt 241\n 2024-04-18 HIV BP 127/82 Wt 229\n 2024-01-19 HIV BP 127/79 Wt 240\n 2023-10-21 HIV BP 117/84 Wt 231\n 2023-07-23 lab review BP 119/86 Wt 235\n 2023-04-24 HIV BP 129/79 Wt 235\n 2023-01-24 HIV BP 116/81 Wt 237\n\nAssessment/Plan:\n • HIV (on ART for 7.9 years; viral load undetectable for 94 months; CD4 count 1109) - well-controlled; currently on bictegravir-emtricitabine-tenofovir 50/200/25 mg. Mr. Price has been under consistent care and has maintained a stable health status.\n • Blood pressure and weight measurements have remained within normal limits, with the most recent reading showing a BP of 120/81 and weight of 232 lbs on January 13, 2025.\n • The patient reported experiencing a minor upper respiratory infection (URI) on July 17, 2024, with a blood pressure of 124/89 and weight of 241 lbs.\n • A comprehensive review of lab results was performed on July 23, 2023, indicating no abnormalities.\n • Mr. Price has a history of tobacco use, having smoked 10 cigarettes per day starting from April 15, 2007, and quitting on August 25, 2024. He has been honest in disclosing this information.\n • Alcohol consumption is minimal, with an intake of approximately one drink per week.\n • The patient's family history includes type 2 diabetes in his mother, who was at the age of 65 and is currently 85 years old and living.\n\nPhysical Examination:\n- General: Alert, oriented, in no acute distress\n- HEENT: Normocephalic, atraumatic, pupils equal and reactive, conjunctivae without injection\n- Neck: Supple, no lymphadenopathy\n- Cardiovascular: Regular rate and rhythm, no murmurs\n- Respiratory: Clear to auscultation bilaterally, no wheezes or crackles\n- Abdomen: Soft, non-tender, no organomegaly\n- Extremities: No edema, pulses intact\n- Neurologic: Cranial nerves II-XII intact, focal deficits\n\nOverall, Mr. Price's HIV is effectively managed, and his overall health status remains stable. Continued adherence to his antiretroviral therapy and regular monitoring is recommended to maintain this control.\n"
